From 190c14f8c7905f4a0da007c94b70db54e00a92e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:49:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 113/116] ChopGimp: blend mode of drop shadows and outer glows
 onto the layers below (behind effects)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As in Photoshop, a drop shadow / outer glow (gegl:dropshadow) is now
composited with its own blend mode (gegl:dropshadow "blend-mode", GEGL
patch 0007) onto what lies below the layer, then the layer with its mode.

- filter stack: a behind filter is taken out of the chain (its node gets
  the chain's output at its place); a chopgimp:behind-knockout node
  (filter output minus input, premultiplied = the shadow knocked out by
  the layer) is kept for it (gimp_filter_stack_set_behind_func())
- layer node: input (backdrop) -> gimp:layer-mode per effect (its mode,
  layer opacity, layer mask as aux2, translate by the layer offset) ->
  layer mode node (app/core/chopgimp-behind-effects.c)
- only for "blend-mode" != normal, filter mode replace, layer not a
  floating selection / pass-through / backdrop-excluding / showing its
  mask; "normal" (all existing files) renders and links as before
- behind filters are not fused, keep their applicator cache, count in
  the drawable's bounding box and in group invalidation; they are chained
  again (normal) while filters are merged / rasterized
- fx cache key: dropshadow "blend-mode" at its default left out (old
  keys stay valid); chopgimp:behind-knockout is level-safe (drafts)
- UI: Mode de fusion above Opacité in Ombre portée / Lueur externe;
  factory settings: Produit (shadow), Écran (outer glow)
- CHOPGIMP_NO_BEHIND_MODES=1: off (every filter chained, as before)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
